business_count":8},{"category":"Nightlife","historical_business_count":5}],"history":[{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Bars, Food, Nightlife, Pubs, Restaurants","shared_category_count":5},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Bars, Food, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":4},{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"Bars, Cajun/Creole, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":4},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Pubs, Restaurants","shared_category_count":4},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"Food","shared_category_count":1}],"text":[{"business_id":"0sfQbEJRvVrLia0IPfptPg","review_id":"I1cct3tIQJGNLAESCLoXLQ","date":"2009-06-25T20:25:54","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9415289759635925,"text_excerpt":"This food was so good. Amazing. Delicious. Ridic. We walk in to charming service and we're the only ones in there (it has only been open 5 weeks and we were in at odd hours). I get my menu and I'm feeling a muffaletta and my mom a burger. We're pretty starvin so we order an appetizer. Now before I describe the food, let me tell you I was not expecting what I got. The place is nice but really casual and funky. Nets on the ceiling, etc. So we order this portabella stuffed mushroom appetizer. It comes out and I'm in awe. The thing is huge and beautiful. Then I dig in and it's DELICIOUS. This is the food I've come to love in Louisiana. The flavor, the spice, it's perfect. Some of the best stu..."},{"business_id":"0sfQbEJRvVrLia0IPfptPg","review_id":"gACrR8-MYTbJiP8Luh1O9Q","date":"2010-06-13T21:40:04","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9367387294769287,"text_excerpt":"Good food and good atmosphere for being on Bourbon Street. Once you enetered, you almost forgot where you were. I had a cajun pasta dish that was completely yummy."},{"business_id":"0sfQbEJRvVrLia0IPfptPg","review_id":"1JF7pVQXu78keMVLwM5cow","date":"2011-10-31T19:45:03","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.935353696346283,"text_excerpt":"Beaudreaux's was the first place we ate after arriving in New Orleans. We had a few hours to kill before we could check into the hotel, so we decided to wander the French Quarter a bit. Beaudreaux's popped up at just the right time, we were hungry! We started with the Boudin balls at the recommendation of our server - they were awesome! I didn't have anything else like it my entire stay in New Orleans. Delicious, dipped in stone ground mustard. I had one of their specialty po boys, made with roasted pork. I don't have a menu to look at so I don't remember what it was called, but it was T-A-S-T-Y. I think this was the only time I didn't have a seafood centric meal, and it was totally worth..."}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
